No worries at all on the delay! I took another look, re-ran the uere models and got the same AIC & Zsq results. I'm not sure how to tweak the uere specification other than to include certain variables in the telemetry object prior to running uere.fit. So for instance to estimate the uere using DOP, Fix Type, and TTF I made sure my data frame included those variables prior to running as.telemetry and checked that an HDOP and class column correctly appears in the telemetry object (in this case classes included 2D in-time, 3D in-time, 2D timeout or 3D timeout). To run an error model using only DOP and TTF, I removed the GPS.fix.type column from the data frame prior to creating the telemetry object and made sure that the telemetry object now shows a HDOP column and class column with classes of in-time or timeout. Is there a step I'm missing?

Thanks,
Christina

