Hi Isabella,

5 seconds is the minimum sampling interval noticed. The median might still be 1.5 minutes. You can see that easily by running summary() on the telemetry object afterwards.

Plot errors like that usually occur when multiple packages are loaded and R becomes confused about which package should handle which object class... which should not happen but it does.
However, in this case the data in the variogram object looks bad. If you can message/email a copy of the data file, then I can take a look at it.

Best,
Chris

